###Pure

// ============================================================
// graph (L0) -- the one profile that makes a class an edge
// ============================================================
// A property graph's relationship with properties has no element of its own in Pure: an Association is two
// properties and nothing else. The element that CAN hold a relationship's properties, identity, mapping and
// constraints is a class, and this profile is how a class says it is one (docs/CYPHER_STUDY_2026_10_15.md §5.6).
// Eight stereotypes and no tags: nothing in the declaration is a string. The engine and Studio compile the profile
// and its applications as they compile any; legend-lite reads them in phase F (compiler/element/GraphEdges) and
// the Cypher island walks a pattern over an edge class as a navigation through its two ends.
//
//   Edge  on a class: the class is a relationship type; its instances are relationships
//   from  on a to-one class-typed property of the edge class (own, inherited or association-injected): the start node
//   to    likewise: the end node
//   type  on a derived property of the edge class whose body is one spelled enumeration value: the relationship type's
//         name (without it, the class's simple name)
//   Open  on a DataSpace (2026-10-17, docs/CYPHER_STUDY_2026_10_15.md §12.45): the DataSpace is a GRAPH a Cypher
//         island reads (`USE g::Graph MATCH ...`: its elements the labels, its execution context the store), and an
//         OPEN one, in GQL's words a graph no graph type constrains (ISO/IEC 39075: a graph with a constraining graph
//         type is CLOSED): a label or a relationship type naming nothing of the graph reads no rows and a property no
//         class declares reads null, as Neo4j reads them. Without it, the model is the graph's type and a name the
//         model lacks is a compile error (the closed reading, docs/SEMANTICS_REGISTER.md S58).
//   Anonymous  on a class (2026-10-17, docs/CYPHER_STUDY_2026_10_15.md §12.61): the class's name is no label. Its
//         instances carry its superclasses' labels alone: a node of several labels is an instance of an anonymous
//         class extending each label's class, a node of none an instance of one extending nothing. Without it a
//         class's simple name is a label its instances carry, and its subclasses' instances too: `labels(n)` lists
//         the class's name and its superclasses', and `MATCH (n:Label)` reads the label's class and its subclasses.
//   nanoseconds  on a DateTime property (2026-10-17, docs/CYPHER_STUDY_2026_10_15.md §12.64): its values are of
//         nanosecond precision (the store's TIMESTAMP_NS column, lite's own type); the Cypher island spells every
//         operation on them over the nanosecond epoch, which DuckDB keeps and a microsecond engine refuses by name.
//   timeOfDay  on a DateTime property (2026-10-17, §12.64): the property holds a time of day as the date-time at it
//         on the epoch day (1970-01-01), the island's own carriage of a time of day finer than a TIME column holds;
//         the island reads it as a time of day (`localtime`) of nanosecond precision. A time of day to the
//         microsecond is a TIME column and a StrictTime property, needing no mark.
Profile graph::graph
{
   stereotypes: [Anonymous, Edge, Open, from, to, type, nanoseconds, timeOfDay];
}
